          "date": "2026-11-08 21:12:01.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21147 doc: add adaptive OST read cache design",
        "message": "LU-21147 doc: add adaptive OST read cache design\n\nThe OSD read cache gates page retention on two static, device-wide\nthresholds: readcache_max_io_mb and readcache_max_filesize.  A shared\nfile larger than readcache_max_filesize is never cached no matter how\nmany clients read it, whereas a small file read by a single client is\ncached even though that client already caches the data locally under a\nDLM PR lock.\n\nAdd Documentation/adaptive-read-cache.txt describing the design of an\nadaptive heat-based OST read cache that tracks per-object distinct\nclient read fan-in in OFD using rotating Bloom filter bins and hands\nthe read-caching verdict to osd-ldiskfs and osd-zfs via dt_bufs_type\nflags.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Jinshan Xiong <jinshanx@google.com>\nAssisted-by: Gemini:gemini-4-argon\nChange-Id: I93827f003eb74b75fa4aec86b1d0390f97f3a5d8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
